WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.319
Week 31: Comparison, Register, and Idiomatic Force. make a nuanced comparison praise or criticize appropriately interpret idioms from context

2
00:00:10.319 --> 00:00:32.871
Read for the situation. El equipo celebró porque el proyecto iba viento en popa, pero una analista pidió tomar las cifras con pinzas. Su cautela dio en el clavo cuando apareció un error. The team celebrated because the project was going very well, but an analyst asked them to treat the figures with caution. Her caution proved exactly right when an error appeared.

3
00:00:32.871 --> 00:00:41.441
Read again for evidence. Identify who acts, what changes, when it happens, and which words establish the relationship between events.

4
00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:47.301
Reading activities. Reading activity 74; Reading activity 75

5
00:00:47.301 --> 00:00:55.082
Retell. Without looking back, give the main idea, three supporting details, and one reasonable inference in Spanish.

6
00:00:55.082 --> 00:01:23.068
Model language. El equipo celebró el avance del proyecto. — The team celebrated the project's progress. Iba viento en popa hasta ese momento. — It was going very well up to that point. Una analista pidió cautela con las cifras. — An analyst asked for caution with the figures. Su advertencia resultó correcta. — Her warning proved correct. Un error apareció poco después. — A mistake appeared shortly after.

7
00:01:23.068 --> 00:01:32.817
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
